import{_ as t,o as a,c as n,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.BUOFcz_J.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Independent plugin backend acceptance","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"records/plugin-split-acceptance.md","filePath":"records/plugin-split-acceptance.md"}'),s={name:"records/plugin-split-acceptance.md"};function r(o,e,c,d,l,p){return a(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Historical record</p><p>This page records what happened on a date, with its observed failures and limits. It is not a requirement for the current implementation. Current behaviour is in <a href="/Rho/docs/reference/status">Status</a>.</p></div><h1 id="independent-plugin-backend-acceptance" tabindex="-1">Independent plugin backend acceptance <a class="header-anchor" href="#independent-plugin-backend-acceptance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Independent plugin backend acceptance&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Updated: 2026-10-16. This record covers the 0.3 package split. API 2.0, <code>r.execute</code> 0.2.0, view contracts 0.2.0 and inert protocol fixtures retain their meanings. No UI was implemented. Earlier <a href="/Rho/docs/records/extraction-acceptance">extraction</a> and <a href="/Rho/docs/records/backend-acceptance">v1 acceptance</a> remain historical evidence.</p><h2 id="delivered-boundary" tabindex="-1">Delivered boundary <a class="header-anchor" href="#delivered-boundary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Delivered boundary&quot;">​</a></h2><p><a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho-plugins/blob/main/docs/PLUGIN-PACKAGES.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Eight independent capability packages</a> own Documents, Files, R, Requirements, Tables, Media, Charts and Agent. Each has its own manifest, version, compiled implementation, descriptor and optional entries. No plugin imports another implementation; Rho injects typed ports. Shared contracts contain schemas and ordinary-file primitives, with no capability state/catalog or R/CSV/MCP dependency. The private source workspace rejects root packing. Only Tables depends on csv-parse; only Agent depends on MCP SDK. Examples and the Agent evaluator are outside the capability tarballs.</p><p>Rho selects finite reviewed packages and exact versions, publishes actual availability, checks required services and wires the selected owners. CLI <code>--plugins</code> controls activation; <code>pack:local --select-plugins</code> also controls which packages are physically included. There is no automatic installation or arbitrary module-path loading. Core&#39;s managed execution and public CLI remain unchanged.</p><h2 id="source-and-component-checks" tabindex="-1">Source and component checks <a class="header-anchor" href="#source-and-component-checks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Source and component checks&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>13/13 Rho tests pass</strong>, including actual HTTP/Core and stdio MCP, original identity across three SIGKILL delivery boundaries, v1/v2 contract fixtures, authentication/scope, drafts/undo, export/restore and resource budgets.</li><li><strong>10/10 plugin tests pass</strong>, covering existing documents, typed keys/nulls, joins, byte integrity, script snapshots, requirements and durable Agent intents, plus independent media/object/context owners and typed bytes without providers.</li><li><strong>2/2 separate native example tests pass</strong>, preserving singleton histogram and spaced Unicode script identity behavior.</li><li><strong>8/8 isolated plugin installations/imports pass</strong>. Each fresh consumer has contracts plus exactly one capability package. CSV and MCP dependencies follow only their owners; installed packages are ordinary directories, not symlinks.</li></ul><p>The removal/reselection test executes an R script once, retains its Core identity, draft/undo, typed table bytes, stable selection and scatter composition, then selects only Documents/Files. Typed reads, chart data, Agent context and new R submissions become unavailable; raw bytes and the identical accepted intent remain readable. Export/restore preserves bytes and drafts while missing typed selection remains explicit. Selecting no plugins still preserves metadata/save; reselecting all permits typed reads and undo without another dispatch or Host.</p><p>An initial new test used the wrong client error property and a component fixture omitted frozen code. Corrected fixtures pass; no execution outcome was changed. The pre-existing scientific trial failures retain their original records.</p><h2 id="installed-composition" tabindex="-1">Installed composition <a class="header-anchor" href="#installed-composition" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Installed composition&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/blob/main/docs/backend-acceptance/v0.3.0.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">immutable 0.3 record</a> freezes both actual npm candidates, nine individual package hashes, source trees/build inputs, production locks, selected example inputs and observed request/resource identities. Both use committed inputs without a local override: Rho <code>2bb6a8a028103bcf465bb80569f4d6f8e8be7f5d</code>, Plugins <code>09b5c7f055ab65ed017cbdbd96abe64273739fb0</code> and unchanged Core <code>d0159da6feb01d1be9e3b4b34b67953241fedfcb</code>.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Actual candidate</th><th>Physical first-party packages</th><th>npm bytes / entries</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Full</td><td>Contracts plus all eight plugins</td><td>6,249,545 / 3,790</td></tr><tr><td>Reduced</td><td>Contracts, Documents and Files</td><td>2,658,922 / 601</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The full tarball SHA256 is <code>e9ced10bc544d20f54ef3c8413c1fffcfdbaefcf303ba25c44fcb3a8da5df875</code>; the reduced tarball SHA256 is <code>81e16aa388bf03ead26e4adbd9a2709816eea693b7325837ce4ab0399b141aae</code>. Both contain the same selected Core bytes. Shared plugin artifacts match exactly across these candidates. They are unsigned local npm tarballs.</p><p>The full candidate was installed outside the source checkouts under a spaced Chinese path. Bin startup without R, private credentials, bundled Core selection, schema/fixture presence and ordinary installed plugin directories passed. The same installed runner then passed:</p><ul><li><strong>Ordinary base-R project:</strong> real linear model, four keyed rows, two-input comparison, PNG/PDF, exported object and project-owned coefficient checks.</li><li><strong>Original paired project:</strong> five DESeq2 fits, 16,139-row typed results and 33 baseline artifacts; 121/121 saved-model observations and 12/12 arithmetic checks; explicit apeglm/dependency preparation, shrinkage with original Wald tests unchanged and a two-input comparison. This bounded trial uses one simulation and does not replace the earlier 200-simulation evidence.</li><li><strong>Recovery:</strong> four computed partial rows survive owned Host loss with the original request/native identity and unknown outcome. Observation closure does not cancel work. Partial export/restore starts no Host or replacement run; separate explicit cancellation confirms native process-group release.</li></ul><p>The reduced candidate was installed in another fresh process. Only Contracts, Documents and Files are physically present; csv-parse and the MCP SDK are absent. The other six selected defaults honestly report missing packages as unavailable. Unicode draft editing, export and bounded project observations work without R or Host startup. It also exercises the actual compiled application with absent optional implementations, beyond activation-only source tests.</p><p>An initial application pack check rejected upstream MCP SDK <code>examples</code> paths. The corrected predicate excludes first-party recipes while allowing the unchanged third-party dependency distribution. That failed candidate remains unaccepted; the two hashes above identify the successful checks and installations.</p><p>Documentation links/anchors and all changed rendered pages were checked. The final evidence/status batch was rendered again after recording these results. Registry publication, signing, other platforms, live R variables and all browser behavior remain outside this scope. Later documentation commits do not rebuild or replace these accepted candidates.</p>',19)])])}const b=t(s,[["render",r]]);export{h as __pageData,b as default};
